# AETHER — Phase 16: Extend the LLM Gateway to the Contextual Intelligence Agents (Sentiment, Macro, Event)

> Bounded, single-phase prompt, same discipline as every prior phase in `docs/Prompts/`. No prior conversation history is available to you — this document is self-contained. Do not touch `flow-agent` or `contrarian-agent` (a separate future phase, deliberately excluded — see Section 8) or anything outside intelligence-agent nodes. Audit first, as always.

---

## 0. Context you must internalize first

AETHER is a no-code visual builder for algorithmic trading agents (Next.js frontend at `apps/web`, FastAPI engine at `apps/engine`, Supabase Postgres). A real LLM gateway (`apps/engine/app/llm/gateway.py`) exists: multi-provider dispatch (Groq, OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Google, Alibaba, Ollama), atomic credit debit/refund against `credit_wallets`, a BYOK (bring-your-own-key) vault (`user_provider_keys`, encrypted at rest, resolved server-side only, never exposed to the browser or persisted in bot graphs), full audit logging to `llm_call_log`, and a hard rule — enforced and tested — that `historical`/`walk-forward`/`monte-carlo` backtests never call a real LLM; only `paper` (capped to the most recent 300 bars) and `live` do. All of this is wired into exactly one node: `TechnicalAnalystNode` (`apps/engine/app/nodes/intelligence_agents/technical_analyst.py`).

Every other Layer III intelligence-agent node — `sentiment-agent`, `macro-agent`, `flow-agent`, `contrarian-agent`, `event-agent` — is still a generic rule-based stub, all routed through the same `UniversalNode` class (`apps/engine/app/nodes/universal.py`) via `create_node_factory(...)` in `apps/engine/app/nodes/registry.py`. `UniversalNode`'s `"agents"` layer branch applies one generic RSI-threshold heuristic to all of them regardless of which specific agent they claim to be — there is currently no differentiation between what a "Sentiment Analyst" and a "Macro Strategist" actually compute.

**Your job this phase:** give `sentiment-agent`, `macro-agent`, and `event-agent` their own dedicated node classes with real, differentiated deterministic logic and real LLM wiring, following the exact hardened pattern already proven on Technical Analyst — but **factor the shared plumbing (credit debit/refund, BYOK resolution, gateway call, logging, redaction) into one reusable base class first**, so you are not copy-pasting ~80 lines of gateway-integration code three more times. Copy-pasting that logic once already produced a real bug in a prior phase (a hardcoded fallback `node_id` because the copy didn't thread context correctly) — a shared base class is not a nice-to-have here, it's the actual fix for a failure mode this project has already hit.

`flow-agent` (needs genuinely different upstream data — order-book/microstructure numbers, not the NewsFeed-shaped stub the other three share) and `contrarian-agent` (needs an existing upstream `Signal` to contest, a fundamentally different node-graph assumption than an independent analyst) are deliberately excluded from this phase — they don't share enough shape with these three to belong in the same batch, and are planned as a separate, later phase.

